```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController()
  fetch(`/api/search?q=${query}`, { signal: controller.signal })
    .then((r) => r.json())
    .then(setResults)
    .catch((err) => {
      if (err.name !== 'AbortError') setError(err)
    })
  return () => controller.abort() // cleanup before next run / unmount
}, [query])
// logs: abort then fetch when query changes — slow response must not win
```

The effect talks to the network after commit. Cleanup aborts the in-flight request so a late response cannot overwrite a newer query. Derived UI stays out of this hook.

