```ts
const proto = { kind: 'row' }
const row = Object.create(proto)
row.id = 1
row.id                         // 1 (own)
row.kind                       // 'row' (prototype)
Object.getPrototypeOf(row) === proto // true

class AppError extends Error {}
const err = new AppError('fail')
err instanceof AppError        // true in this realm

Array.isArray(data)            // not data instanceof Array
el.nodeType === 1              // not el instanceof HTMLElement
const map = markRaw(new google.maps.Map(el))
```

`Object.create` is the chain without `class`. `class` adds a constructor and `instanceof`. Realm-safe checks and `markRaw` are the production part of the same answer.

