```ts
const src = { user: { role: 'admin' }, rows: [{ id: 1 }] }
const shallow = { ...src }
shallow.user.role = 'guest'
src.user.role // 'guest' — nested ref shared

const detached = structuredClone(toRaw(src))
detached.user.role = 'viewer'
src.user.role // still 'guest'

// JSON.stringify drops undefined and Date-as-Date
```

Spread copied one level. Nested `user` stayed shared. `structuredClone(toRaw(src))` detaches; that is the copy you send off-thread or persist, not the copy you make on every keystroke.

