```ts
onMounted(() => {
  const onResize = () => updateLayout()
  window.addEventListener('resize', onResize) // ❌ leaked after leave
})

onMounted(() => {
  const ac = new AbortController()
  window.addEventListener('resize', onResize, { signal: ac.signal })
  const stop = watch(filters, fetchList)
  onScopeDispose(() => {
    ac.abort()
    stop()
  })
})
```

The first snippet pins the component (and anything the handler closes over) for the session. The second pairs the listener and the `watch` with the scope. Two heap snapshots plus Retainers prove the `Detached` node is gone.

