example.en:
```ts
function loadUser(id: string) {
  return getUser(id)
    .then((user) => getPosts(user.id).then((posts) => ({ user, posts })))
    .catch((err) => {
      reportError(err)
      throw err
    })
}

async function loadUserAsync(id: string) {
  try {
    const user = await getUser(id)
    const posts = await getPosts(user.id)
    return { user, posts }
  } catch (err) {
    reportError(err)
    throw err
  }
}
// Both: pending → fulfilled { user, posts } or rejected. Same contract.
```

The `.then` chain and `async`/`await` are the same Promise contract. `try/catch` around `await` is `.catch`. Neither version cancels; pass `AbortSignal` into `getUser` / `getPosts`.

