```css
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; } /* width includes padding+border */
.card {
  width: 320px;
  padding: 16px;
  border: 2px solid #111;
  /* content-box would be 320+32+4 = 356px and overflow a 320px grid cell */
}
.stack > * + * { margin-top: 1rem; } /* collapse in normal flow; not on flex/grid items */
.btn:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--focus); /* does not add width */
  /* border: 2px solid var(--focus); would grow the box and shift layout */
}
```

`border-box` keeps the card at 320px. Sibling `margin-top` can collapse in a stacked flow; a flex column will not. Outline is the focus ring that does not blow the budget.

