```tsx
function Row({ user, selectedId }: { user: User; selectedId: string }) {
  // ❌ const [u, setU] = useState(user) — drifts when parent passes a new user
  const isOn = user.id === selectedId // derive in render
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false) // local UI this row owns
  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    if (open) measure(el.current) // before paint — rare
  }, [open])
  // useEffect for outside-world sync lives in the sibling question
  return <li data-on={isOn}>{user.name}</li>
}
// key={user.id} remounts this state when the row identity changes
```

Props stay read-only; derived flags stay in render; `useState` holds only UI this row owns. `useLayoutEffect` is the measure path. Effects and cleanup are the sibling topic.

